*actor* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

''actor(function)''
''actor(function, arg)''
''actor(function, arg1, arg2, ...)''

Spawns a new concurrent actor that executes ''function'' with the given ''arg''uments. Returns the handle of the new actor.

The spawned actor runs in its own interpreter instance with its own handle registry and a deep copy of all non-builtin symbols visible at spawn time. The spawner and the actor operate on fully separate data. For more information about the model see ''chippy doc concurrency''.

Every spawned actor handle must eventually be passed to ''wait(handle)'' to release its bookkeeping.

*Parameters:*
- ''function'': Function to run in the actor
- ''arg1, arg2, ...'': Arguments passed to the function

*Returns:*
- Number: Actor handle

*Errors:*
- Runtime error if first argument is not a function
- Runtime error if argument count does not match the function signature
